@WouterJ I get it, when I submit a form, where one of the values, provided by the client, is `null`.

I use FOSRest to allow the user to send body-data in `application/json` instead of `application/x-www-form-urlencoded`. When the user now submits `null` for one of the fields, the form cannot be debugged anymore.

It works for all other types that are unusual for `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` (bool, empty array, integer, what more?) - it just fails at `null`.

I had the same problem.

The cause was a FormEvents::SUBMIT changed the form. example:

The _setParent(null)_ gives me the profiler error

``` php
 public function foo(FormEvent $event)
    {
        $data = $event->getData();
        $form = $event->getForm();
        $form->setParent(null);
    }
```

Maybe this helps.
